# rena0-jump-climb — F1-3 fixture, P2-7 jump family (height is bounded only by the meter)
#
# Source: row 41's climb adds +0.2/tick to vy while jump is held, capped at 6.0/tick, and
# spends 10 of the action meter per climbing tick (FUN_0043ffc0 case 0x29). There is NO
# altitude cap anywhere in the air chain — the function an earlier note cited for a
# "flight cap" (FUN_00421bd0) only writes spawn X/Z and a 1000.0 respawn Y. So holding
# the button climbs while the meter lasts, and the meter is what ends the climb.
#
# The port used to pin vy at 12/tick, clamp the position at a 420-unit kFlyMaxAlt AND stop the
# climb on a 1.2 s kFlyTimeSec budget — which cut it with ~28% of the bar still full. None of
# those exists in the recovered chain: the climb ends when the meter empties. Measured on the
# corrected path, the height passes the old cap and peaks at 621 as the bar reaches zero.
combo 0 0
seed 5489
spawn 0 0 0 0
spawn 1 0 0 2000
collision open-field
input 0 JUMP
expect 40 y 246
expect 60 y 366
expect 80 y 486
expect 80 charge_gauge 200
expect 100 charge_gauge 0
expect 100 y 606
expect 120 y 621
expect 140 y 436
